    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d391">

                <pb facs="1170" n="1020" xml:id="pg1020"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 3123/7.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Swedish
                        Chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-12-09"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 42.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received with sincere regret your
                    note of the 8th instant anouncing the death of His Majesty King Oscar II of
                    Sweden, which took place at the royal castle at Stockholm on yesterday
                    morning.</p>
                <p>A telegram was received at an early hour yesterday from the minister of the
                    United States at Stockholm announcing His Majesty’s death.</p>
                <p>The President at once sent a telegram to His Majesty Gustavus V, reading as
                        follows.<anchor n="a" xml:id="d391-f1"/></p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
